      "id": "1cdbd0b1-7016-48cf-8dff-7e3a91a1e84d",
      "object": "block",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": {
        "rich_text": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": {
              "content": "Appa made this sambar every Sunday morning. He'd wake up before anyone else and start the toor dal while listening to MS Subbulakshmi on the kitchen radio. The whole house would smell like tamarind and curry leaves by 8am. He always said you can't rush the tamarind. He'd taste it ten times, adjusting the salt each round, using every spoon in the kitchen. Amma used to complain about the cleanup. He bought his drumstick fresh from the Indian store on University Ave in Berkeley. The handwriting on the recipe card is his, crossed out and corrected over years of making it."
            },
            "plain_text": "Appa made this sambar every Sunday morning. He'd wake up before anyone else and start the toor dal while listening to MS Subbulakshmi on the kitchen radio. The whole house would smell like tamarind and curry leaves by 8am. He always said you can't rush the tamarind. He'd taste it ten times, adjusting the salt each round, using every spoon in the kitchen. Amma used to complain about the cleanup. He bought his drumstick fresh from the Indian store on University Ave in Berkeley. The handwriting on the recipe card is his, crossed out and corrected over years of making it."
          }
        ]
      },
